{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implement the increment as part of the Spring XD (Spring Extreme Data) project, which is the implied target based on the user stories (XD containers, modules, streams, source/sink model).",
    "Use Kafka 0.8.x/0.9.x simple (low-level) Consumer API for U2, with manual offset management and explicit partition assignment to satisfy the deterministic control requirement.",
    "Implement U1 ingestion via a JDBC-based source module that supports batch fetching, combined with three sink modules: HDFS (using Hadoop FileSystem API), HAWQ and GPDB (both via JDBC with COPY/EXTERNAL TABLE bulk loading).",
    "Expose U3 as a new admin REST endpoint in the Admin UI / Controller layer using Spring MVC, with multipart file upload and an in-process file-based module repository that hot-deploys jars to the container(s).",
    "Build U4 as a standalone Spring Boot-based sample application in its own GitHub repository, with docker-compose scripts to provision a single-node XD cluster with Kafka and Zookeeper.",
    "Implement U5 (generator) and U6 (perf-meter) as standard XD source/sink modules using the existing XD Module SPI, with command-line option parsing via the XD OptionsMetadata mechanism.",
    "U7 is treated primarily as a validation/verification activity (compose the stream on a singlenode container) plus minor glue work, not a separate feature implementation.",
    "U8 test coverage implemented as JUnit 4 tests using XD's existing test harness (single-node embedded container), with Gradle/Maven Surefire integration for CI execution.",
    "All modules will be packaged as uber-jars (matching the existing XD module convention) so they can be pushed via U3's REST API.",
    "Java 8 is assumed as the development target (consistent with Spring XD 1.x baseline; Spring Framework 6.0/Java 17 in the spec preamble is a generic framework description, not the constraint for this increment)."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer (the estimator) performs all work, so all activities are sequential and self-contained.",
    "Spring XD base code, XD build system, and module SPI are already in place; this increment only adds new modules/endpoints on top.",
    "Kafka, HDFS, HAWQ, and GPDB are available as external systems for integration testing but their installation is not part of this effort.",
    "Unit and integration test infrastructure (embedded XD container, test harnesses) already exists; only new test classes are authored.",
    "Effort includes design, implementation, unit tests, integration tests, debugging, and basic documentation per activity. CI pipeline configuration is included in A14.",
    "Effort values represent focused development work-hours (no meetings, breaks, or unrelated overhead).",
    "Reasonable buffer for defect fixing is included inside each implementation activity rather than as a separate contingency line.",
    "The 'spike' in U2 is treated as 12 hours of study + documentation; the actual implementation is a separate activity (A7).",
    "HAWQ and GPDB sinks share significant code (both are Greenplum-derived); A5 is therefore smaller than A4 reflecting reuse.",
    "The sample app (U4) is a small, demonstrative project, not a production-grade application."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and overall design",
      "activity_description": "Review all eight user stories, define the module inventory, design module SPI extensions (option metadata, lifecycle hooks), and produce a high-level technical design document covering module packaging, REST contract, and Kafka source/sink boundaries."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - JDBC batch source module",
      "activity_description": "Implement a generic JDBC source module supporting configurable query, fetch size, batch size, and column-to-tuple conversion. Includes connection pooling config, error handling, and unit tests with an embedded H2 database."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1 - HDFS sink module",
      "activity_description": "Implement an HDFS sink module that writes incoming payloads to HDFS in a configurable directory with rolling file support. Uses Hadoop FileSystem API, supports text and sequence file formats, with integration tests against a mini-HDFS cluster."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U1 - HAWQ sink module",
      "activity_description": "Implement a HAWQ sink using JDBC with bulk loading (via external table or COPY where appropriate). Includes connection config, batch insert, and integration tests against a HAWQ test instance (or Greenplum-compatible mock)."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U1 - GPDB sink module",
      "activity_description": "Implement a GPDB sink reusing the HAWQ infrastructure where possible, adjusting for GPDB-specific SQL/loading differences. Includes lightweight unit tests and a smoke integration test."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Kafka simple consumer API spike",
      "activity_description": "Study the Kafka simple (low-level) Consumer API: partition assignment strategies, offset commit patterns, rebalancing, error handling, and thread safety. Produce a written findings document with a recommended approach and next-step implementation plan."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Kafka simple consumer source implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Kafka source module on top of the simple Consumer API per the spike's findings. Includes deterministic offset and partition assignment, restart-safe offset persistence, and unit/integration tests against an embedded Kafka broker."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U3 - REST API for custom module upload",
      "activity_description": "Add a multipart REST endpoint to the XD Admin Controller that accepts an uber-jar, validates it, stores it in the module repository, and triggers hot-deployment to the target container(s). Includes controller, service, repository extension, error handling, basic auth assumption documented, and integration tests."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Sample app GitHub project (XD + Kafka)",
      "activity_description": "Create a standalone GitHub project: Spring Boot shell, docker-compose for XD singlenode + Kafka + Zookeeper, sample stream definition using Kafka source/sink, README with provisioning steps, and one end-to-end smoke test script."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Generator source module",
      "activity_description": "Implement a generator source module with options --numMsgs, --msgSize, --numThreads. Produces synthetic messages of a fixed byte size at a configurable rate. Includes option metadata, multi-threaded message production, and unit tests."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Perf-meter sink module",
      "activity_description": "Implement a perf-meter sink that records timestamp, message count, and instantaneous message rate to the standard container log every N messages (default 1000). Uses XD's logger output channel and includes unit tests verifying rate calculation and log formatting."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Stream composition verification (generator | perf-meter)",
      "activity_description": "Verify that the generator source and perf-meter sink can be composed into a single stream on a singlenode container. Includes a 1M-message run script, log inspection to confirm rate values, and any minor glue work needed for the composition."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Test coverage for Kafka source and sink modules",
      "activity_description": "Author unit and integration tests for the existing Kafka source and sink modules (not just the new simple-consumer source). Cover happy path, offset persistence, rebalancing, partition failure, and serialization edge cases. Add the new tests to the CI build matrix."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Cross-module integration testing, CI wiring, and bug fixing",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end integration scenarios combining U1 ingestion, U2 Kafka source, U3 module upload, and U7 perf stream. Wire new modules/tests into the Gradle build, fix defects found during integration, and verify CI green."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and release notes",
      "activity_description": "Write user-facing documentation for new modules (generator, perf-meter, JDBC source, HDFS/HAWQ/GPDB sinks, REST upload endpoint), update the reference guide, add JavaDoc, and produce release notes summarizing U1-U8 deliverables."
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 210
  }
}
```

